2451
01:36:14.078 --> 01:36:15.355
<v JEFFERSON>No, no. Go ahead.

2452
01:36:15.355 --> 01:36:16.952
<v HANDY>My house is still there.

2453
01:36:16.952 --> 01:36:18.867
<v JEFFERSON>No . . . They did cut us down.

2454
01:36:18.867 --> 01:36:23.337
<v JOURDAN>They did cut you Kat, but the way you said it wasn't just right.

2455
01:36:23.337 --> 01:36:24.295
But that’s alright.

2456
01:36:24.295 --> 01:36:25.253
<v ARSENEAULT>The Victorian style?

2457
01:36:25.253 --> 01:36:27.169
I always look at that one.

2458
01:36:27.169 --> 01:36:29.084
<v JOURDAN>Anything else you need to know?

2459
01:36:29.084 --> 01:36:31.000
Because I got to run.

2460
01:36:31.000 --> 01:36:32.280
<v PORTER>Get back to work.

2461
01:36:32.280 --> 01:36:35.160
<v ARSENEAULT>We can always reschedule too if you need to.

2462
01:36:35.160 --> 01:36:38.040
I mean I have a lot of questions here.

2463
01:36:38.040 --> 01:36:41.240
I guess I could ask one kind of further back.

2464
01:36:41.240 --> 01:36:43.480
So Martin Luther King and President Kennedy.

2465
01:36:43.480 --> 01:36:46.680
Do y'all remember . . . What do y'all remember about that time?

2466
01:36:46.680 --> 01:36:47.000
<v JOURDAN>Yeah.

2467
01:36:47.000 --> 01:36:47.320
Violent.

2468
01:36:47.320 --> 01:36:50.200
<v HANDY>I was in sixth grade when Kennedy got killed.

2469
01:36:50.200 --> 01:36:51.800
<v JOURDAN>I was in third grade.

2470
01:36:51.800 --> 01:36:53.720
<v LATOUR>I remember when Kennedy got killed.

2471
01:36:53.720 --> 01:36:55.320
It was the saddest thing.

2472
01:36:55.320 --> 01:36:56.600
<v JOURDAN>Where you was and . . .

2473
01:36:56.600 --> 01:36:57.880
<v JEFFERSON>We were at school.

2474
01:36:57.880 --> 01:36:59.800
<v HANDY>It was a very sad day.

2475
01:36:59.800 --> 01:37:03.000
The whole school was . . . We were all broke up.

2476
01:37:03.000 --> 01:37:09.222
<v LATOUR>You know what I always attribute that . . . I compare it to in my mind that's how I have it set.

2477
01:37:09.222 --> 01:37:12.333
Like when my daddy died and when President Kennedy died.

2478
01:37:12.333 --> 01:37:16.378
It was three years apart, but to me that was the same event.

2479
01:37:16.378 --> 01:37:17.311
<v HANDY>Two honest men.

2480
01:37:17.311 --> 01:37:18.556
They were honest men.

2481
01:37:18.556 --> 01:37:20.111
<v LATOUR>You know what I'm saying?

2482
01:37:20.111 --> 01:37:26.956
Then Martin Luther King when he got killed too that was just . . . For somebody to take his life that was really sad.

2483
01:37:26.956 --> 01:37:29.444
And his children to be without a daddy.

2484
01:37:29.444 --> 01:37:30.378
I guess because . . .

2485
01:37:30.378 --> 01:37:35.356
<v HANDY>We were out of a daddy at an early age so it kind of affected us.

2486
01:37:35.356 --> 01:37:41.267
<v PORTER>It kind of made us think about what the kids were going through because we had been through it.

2487
01:37:41.267 --> 01:37:42.822
<v HANDY>We could feel they pain.

2488
01:37:42.822 --> 01:37:46.556
I think it's really the worst for somebody to take they life.

2489
01:37:46.556 --> 01:37:46.867
<v UNIDENTIFIED PERSON>Carol.

2490
01:37:46.867 --> 01:37:52.156
<v HANDY>Because they just . . . You know they was just doing what God had sent them here to do.

2491
01:37:52.156 --> 01:37:56.511
<v JEFFERSON>I think it was just a hateful . . . It showed you how much hate was . . .

2492
01:37:56.511 --> 01:37:57.133
<v HANDY>People . . . yeah.

2493
01:37:57.133 --> 01:37:58.378
<v JEFFERSON>Actually in the world.

2494
01:37:58.378 --> 01:37:59.000
<v HANDY>America.

2495
01:37:59.000 --> 01:38:00.530
<v LATOUR>And have we really changed?

2496
01:38:00.530 --> 01:38:02.060
<v HANDY>We haven't really changed yeah.

2497
01:38:02.060 --> 01:38:08.486
<v LATOUR>Because to me what's going on with [Donald] Trump is only bringing up how much hate there is in the world.

2498
01:38:08.486 --> 01:38:15.831
For all the people whose following him they are hate seekers and mongers because he's addressing it, but they the ones that's following him.

2499
01:38:15.831 --> 01:38:17.361
You know what I mean?

2500
01:38:17.361 --> 01:38:20.115
So that's showing still there's a lot of hate.

2501
01:38:20.115 --> 01:38:22.257
<v ARSENEAULT>Do you have any memories of protesting?

2502
01:38:22.257 --> 01:38:25.011
I know you said Mossville . . . You didn't really leave.

2503
01:38:25.011 --> 01:38:26.847
You had everything you needed here.

2504
01:38:26.847 --> 01:38:27.765
<v LATOUR>Yeah we protested.

2505
01:38:27.765 --> 01:38:33.273
<v HANDY>But we don't want it on record. [laughs] If we tell you we may have to kill you.

2506
01:38:33.273 --> 01:38:35.415
<v PORTER>So what happened while I was gone?

2507
01:38:35.415 --> 01:38:36.639
What you laughing at?

2508
01:38:36.639 --> 01:38:37.251
<v KIM MCKEE>Y'all crying?

2509
01:38:37.251 --> 01:38:38.781
<v JEFFERSON>Get out of here Kim.

2510
01:38:38.781 --> 01:38:41.842
<v HANDY>I told her . . . She say if we had any protests.

2511
01:38:41.842 --> 01:38:45.514
I said if we tell you we might have to kill you.

2512
01:38:45.514 --> 01:38:47.656
<v LATOUR>You not supposed to be in here.

2513
01:38:47.656 --> 01:38:48.268
<v MCKEE>I know.

2514
01:38:48.268 --> 01:38:48.880
Y'all crying?

2515
01:38:48.880 --> 01:38:49.492
<v HANDY>No girl.

2516
01:38:49.492 --> 01:38:50.104
We good.

2517
01:38:50.104 --> 01:38:50.716
<v MCKEE>Y'all crying.

2518
01:38:50.716 --> 01:38:55.000
<v PORTER>We close it down and do it again and finish what you need?

2519
01:38:55.000 --> 01:38:58.846
<v ARSENEAULT>I'll just ask you what your . . . What are you going to miss most about Mossville?

2520
01:38:58.846 --> 01:39:00.128
And then we can close.

2521
01:39:00.128 --> 01:39:00.641
<v HANDY>Old house.

2522
01:39:00.641 --> 01:39:03.205
<v PORTER>Grandmother’s old house and our house where we were raised.

2523
01:39:03.205 --> 01:39:05.000
<v HANDY>Because we knew it was there.

2524
01:39:05.000 --> 01:39:09.228
<v PORTER>I'm miss this because my husband built the church, so I'll miss having

2525
01:39:09.228 --> 01:39:10.203
<c.p>the church here.

2526
01:39:10.203 --> 01:39:14.756
And this was our mother’s property that the family donated to build a church.

2527
01:39:14.756 --> 01:39:20.610
That's a big . . . We called ourselves doing something that would be in her remembrance and now it's being . . .

2528
01:39:20.610 --> 01:39:21.260
<v HANDY>Taken down.

2529
01:39:21.260 --> 01:39:25.488
So it's just the memories, but you can have them in your heart.

2530
01:39:25.488 --> 01:39:25.813
<v PORTER>Yeah.

2531
01:39:25.813 --> 01:39:28.740
<v HANDY>And when we pass you don't see the objects.

2532
01:39:28.740 --> 01:39:30.691
<v JOURDAN>Don't even look like Mossville anymore.

2533
01:39:30.691 --> 01:39:31.016
<v HANDY>Yeah.

2534
01:39:31.016 --> 01:39:34.268
It make you wonder what . . . You kind of get lost.

2535
01:39:34.268 --> 01:39:34.919
What's that?

2536
01:39:34.919 --> 01:39:35.894
Mr. Such-and-such yard?

2537
01:39:35.894 --> 01:39:39.797
<v PORTER>So if there's anything else real, real you need to ask us . . .

2538
01:39:39.797 --> 01:39:44.024
<v ARSENEAULT>We can . . . because I think we got a lot of good stuff today.

2539
01:39:44.024 --> 01:39:45.000
<v LATOUR>We don't . . .

2540
01:39:45.000 --> 01:39:49.941
<v ARSENEAULT>It's almost two hours and I know we all got to . . . Need to go.

2541
01:39:49.941 --> 01:39:52.412
<v PORTER>He got to get back to work.

2542
01:39:52.412 --> 01:39:56.647
<v ARSENEAULT>I just have . . . I thought it was only going to be three.

2543
01:39:56.647 --> 01:39:59.471
<v LATOUR>You need to sign one of those papers.

2544
01:39:59.471 --> 01:40:01.941
<v ARSENEAULT>So if you . . . Before you leave yes.

2545
01:40:01.941 --> 01:40:03.706
If you could sign this.

2546
01:40:03.706 --> 01:40:12.176
And anything else you wanted to say before we close up and then I can just kind of contact you about follow ups later.

2547
01:40:12.176 --> 01:40:15.353
Anything else you want to get on the record?

2548
01:40:15.353 --> 01:40:19.235
<v LATOUR>Well as far as I'm concerned we were raised in Mossville.

2549
01:40:19.235 --> 01:40:23.118
We had good times here; we had some sad times here.

2550
01:40:23.118 --> 01:40:31.235
But to me with the way we were raised anywhere we are . . . Anywhere one of us is the rest of us there too.

2551
01:40:31.235 --> 01:40:31.941
We're family.

2552
01:40:31.941 --> 01:40:36.176
So we can be in any community but family is within you.

2553
01:40:36.176 --> 01:40:37.941
It's not just a place.

2554
01:40:37.941 --> 01:40:39.353
It's something within you.

2555
01:40:39.353 --> 01:40:47.471
So I think we had good times and I think that the people as a whole we should have start fighting for Mossville . . .

2556
01:40:47.471 --> 01:40:48.529
<v HANDY>A long time . . .

2557
01:40:48.529 --> 01:40:49.941
<v LATOUR>. . . before Sasol came through.

2558
01:40:49.941 --> 01:40:54.529
We should have fought years ago when they wanted to close our school.

2559
01:40:54.529 --> 01:40:57.706
That’s when the fight should have start taking place.

2560
01:40:57.706 --> 01:41:03.000
But I think we've learned great life lessons here and we'll never forget it.

2561
01:41:03.000 --> 01:41:07.714
<v HANDY>And I think that it was just like being abandoned again.

2562
01:41:07.714 --> 01:41:09.000
You know after

2563
01:41:09.000 --> 01:41:12.429
<c.p>we . . . I was abandoned when my daddy died.

2564
01:41:12.429 --> 01:41:15.429
And that was not of his choice.

2565
01:41:15.429 --> 01:41:17.143
<v PORTER>See you later Preston.

2566
01:41:17.143 --> 01:41:21.000
<v HANDY>When they took the school that was another abandonment.

2567
01:41:21.000 --> 01:41:23.571
And now they've taken the community.

2568
01:41:23.571 --> 01:41:32.143
So that's . . . It just keeps coming up and so the thing that I regret most is not coming back here.

2569
01:41:32.143 --> 01:41:39.429
And I could have became the mayor and I could have fought for the people of Mossville.

2570
01:41:39.429 --> 01:41:41.143
That's my biggest regret.

2571
01:41:41.143 --> 01:41:43.286
That I never came back.

2572
01:41:43.286 --> 01:41:51.000
<v PORTER>And I lived in Sulphur since I got married and it’s been forty-seven years I've been in Sulphur.

2573
01:41:51.000 --> 01:41:54.857
So I come to Mossville church all the time.

2574
01:41:54.857 --> 01:41:57.429
Good memories is in my heart.

2575
01:41:57.429 --> 01:41:59.571
<v JEFFERSON>Well I left here 1978.

2576
01:41:59.571 --> 01:42:06.000
So I just moved back ten years ago and so I really wasn't in Mossville.

2577
01:42:06.000 --> 01:42:08.143
I was in Lake Charles.

2578
01:42:08.143 --> 01:42:15.000
But Mossville was a good place to grow up because it was a lot of love.

2579
01:42:15.000 --> 01:42:27.429
And in our little circle you always had someone that was going to look out for you because you had a cousin here an aunt here a grandmother there.

2580
01:42:27.429 --> 01:42:31.286
What's the . . . And I'm glad it wasn't . . . in Mossville.

2581
01:42:31.286 --> 01:42:33.000
In the city.

2582
01:42:33.000 --> 01:42:34.250
<v PORTER>And you know what?

2583
01:42:34.250 --> 01:42:37.062
We have in our family . . . and I'm not bragging,

2584
01:42:37.062 --> 01:42:42.688
but in our family we didn't get into all that but he had a daughter that's a lawyer.

2585
01:42:42.688 --> 01:42:44.250
Emma's daughter is a doctor.

2586
01:42:44.250 --> 01:42:47.688
And then we got three that's administrators in the school system.

2587
01:42:47.688 --> 01:42:49.562
And all of them got education.

2588
01:42:49.562 --> 01:42:52.688
Because I have a son that has a doctorate degree.

2589
01:42:52.688 --> 01:42:54.875
I have a daughter that's a nurse.

2590
01:42:54.875 --> 01:42:56.125
Another work in surgery.

2591
01:42:56.125 --> 01:43:00.500
So we raised our kids to have the same strive for what you want

2592
01:43:00.500 --> 01:43:01.750
<c.p>to do in life.

2593
01:43:01.750 --> 01:43:03.000
<v ARSENEAULT>The work ethic.

2594
01:43:03.000 --> 01:43:03.217
<v JOURDAN>Right.

2595
01:43:03.217 --> 01:43:05.826
<v PORTER>So that's why I said we didn't get into all that, but . . .

2596
01:43:05.826 --> 01:43:06.043
<v JOURDAN>Right.

2597
01:43:06.043 --> 01:43:09.087
Yeah I thought that's what we were going to get into but we didn't.

2598
01:43:09.087 --> 01:43:11.696
<v ARSENEAULT>Well I will have to schedule a follow up with you guys.

2599
01:43:11.696 --> 01:43:13.217
<v PORTER>She can come back if she want.

2600
01:43:13.217 --> 01:43:16.478
<v JOURDAN>Yeah we like to tell the story of kids growing up and going on and . . .

2601
01:43:16.478 --> 01:43:17.348
<v ARSENEAULT>Those are my favorite.

2602
01:43:17.348 --> 01:43:18.000
<v JOURDAN>Doing better.

2603
01:43:18.000 --> 01:43:22.133
<v PORTER>So we really . . . In the history we need to have that about our kids.

2604
01:43:22.133 --> 01:43:22.429
<v ARSENEAULT>Yeah.

2605
01:43:22.429 --> 01:43:26.857
<v JEFFERSON>And if we get all the pictures together and make copies we can take it . . .

2606
01:43:26.857 --> 01:43:29.810
<v PORTER>That’s what we need to do we need to copy.

2607
01:43:29.810 --> 01:43:30.105
<v JOURDAN>Yeah.

2608
01:43:30.105 --> 01:43:32.171
That’s what I just give Emma mine.

2609
01:43:32.171 --> 01:43:34.238
<v PORTER>Just give them a copy of it.

2610
01:43:34.238 --> 01:43:36.895
<v HANDY>Because my son is a minister at his church.

2611
01:43:36.895 --> 01:43:41.619
<v JOURDAN>Yeah and I grew up with the horses and all that, and I'm still racing horses.

2612
01:43:41.619 --> 01:43:43.095
<v HANDY>He won the championship in [ . . .?].

2613
01:43:43.095 --> 01:43:46.343
<v PORTER>And we had some boys that won some state championship rodeos.

2614
01:43:46.343 --> 01:43:46.933
<v HANDY>Champion rodeos.

2615
01:43:46.933 --> 01:43:49.000
Yeah our kids are very active.

2616
01:43:49.000 --> 01:43:52.607
<v LATOUR>This is the old days, but they been racing so long.

2617
01:43:52.607 --> 01:43:53.918
<v ARSENEAULT>Wow look how beautiful . . .

2618
01:43:53.918 --> 01:43:56.213
<v LATOUR>This one was just the other day.

2619
01:43:56.213 --> 01:43:58.508
<v HANDY>Oh you won the other day babe?

2620
01:43:58.508 --> 01:44:00.475
<v LATOUR>And look his grandbaby on there.

2621
01:44:00.475 --> 01:44:01.787
<v ARSENEAULT>Oh look how cute.

2622
01:44:01.787 --> 01:44:03.098
<v MCKEE>Did they tell you . . .

2623
01:44:03.098 --> 01:44:04.738
<v ARSENEAULT>Well thank y'all so much.

2624
01:44:04.738 --> 01:44:06.377
We can stop it now.

2625
01:44:06.377 --> 01:44:06.705
<v PORTER>Okay.

2626
01:44:06.705 --> 01:44:09.000
<v MCKEE>Did they tell you that they . . .

2627
01:44:09.000 --> 01:44:09.429
<c.p>[End Tape 4625.

2628
01:44:09.429 --> 01:44:09.857
End Session I.]
